{"id":"a1a16cd0a85389409e3f0f52cd2076819a799512","axis":"silent","repo":"appwrite/appwrite","sha":"a1a16cd0a85389409e3f0f52cd2076819a799512","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"packages/cache/docs/versioning.md","lines":["@@ -8,4 +8,6 @@ Redis, Redis multiplexing and in-process Memory support this capability. Wrapper"," "," These tokens reject stale fills; they do not elect a single database-fetch winner. Writer registrations and their lifecycle belong to the database protocol."," ","-Cache 6.0/database 9.0 require a coordinated drain/clear upgrade. Cache 6.1 adds an explicit temporary `Cache::legacy()` facade for the database 9.1 rolling bridge instead. That facade preserves the cache-5 Redis wire format and numeric leases solely for migration; ordinary cache operations never fall back to it. It uses the same adapter, pools and circuit breaker. No opaque fields are written into legacy hashes. Roll the database bridge through legacy reads + dual invalidation, v2 reads + dual invalidation, then v2 only; verify each fleet/in-flight-write barrier before advancing. Keep v2 keys isolated and preserve their namespace during eventual bridge removal. See the database migration documentation for rollback limits. No additional state service is required. A successful post-commit invalidation is still necessary; durable replay of lost invalidations is separate work.","+The temporary legacy numeric-generation facade and Redis scripts are removed. Applications completing the database 9.1 bridge migration must keep their existing key namespace: `$cache->withNamespace('v2:')` shares data, versions and invalidations with bridge clients already in v2 mode. Pass that same view to every database/query-cache user. Purge recordings retain logical keys for semantic replay; the namespace is applied once by the receiving cache. `flush()` remains a whole-backend operation.","+","+Remove migration flags only after the v2-only code has reached the complete fleet, including ad-hoc Jobs and draining processes. Never return to legacy readers after contraction. No cache flush or additional state service is required. A successful post-commit invalidation remains necessary; durable replay of lost invalidations is separate work."],"additions":3,"deletions":1,"truncated":false},{"path":"packages/cache/src/Adapter/CircuitBreaker.php","lines":["@@ -9,7 +9,7 @@"," use Utopia\\CircuitBreaker\\CircuitBreaker as UtopiaCircuitBreaker;"," use Utopia\\Telemetry\\Adapter as Telemetry;"," ","-class CircuitBreaker implements Adapter, Feature\\Batchable, Feature\\Telemetry, \\Utopia\\Cache\\Feature\\Versioned, \\Utopia\\Cache\\Feature\\Legacy","+class CircuitBreaker implements Adapter, Feature\\Batchable, Feature\\Telemetry, \\Utopia\\Cache\\Feature\\Versioned"," {","     public function __construct(","         private readonly Adapter $adapter,","@@ -166,58 +166,6 @@ public function setTelemetry(Telemetry $telemetry): void","         }","     }"," ","-    public function getGeneration(string $key): string","-    {","-        /** @var string $result */","-        $result = $this->breaker->call(","-            open: fn (): never => throw new Unavailable('Legacy cache unavailable'),","-            close: function () use ($key): string {","-                if (! $this->adapter instanceof \\Utopia\\Cache\\Feature\\Legacy) {","-                    throw new Unavailable('Legacy migration requires Redis');","-                }","-","-                return $this->adapter->getGeneration($key);","-            },","-        );","-","-        return $result;","-    }","-","-    /** @param array<int|string, mixed>|string $data */","-    public function saveWithGeneration(string $key, array|string $data, string $hash, string $generation, int $ttl = 0): bool","-    {","-        /** @var bool $result */","-        $result = $this->breaker->call(","-            open: fn (): never => throw new Unavailable('Legacy cache unavailable'),","-            close: function () use ($key, $data, $hash, $genera